subject: fix(cowork-settings): return structured error on config read failure (GAP-P3-33)

writeSkipApprovals previously returned { error: e.code } for non-ENOENT
read failures, leaking raw error codes (EACCES, EBUSY, etc.) to callers
with no context. Callers could not distinguish permission denied from I/O
errors.

Now returns { error: 'config_read_failed', detail: e.message, code: e.code }
so the UI and downstream consumers can render meaningful diagnostics.

Also exports writeSkipApprovals and getWriteRoot for testability.

Regression test covers EACCES, EBUSY, ENOENT (normal first-run), and an
anti-false-positive assertion that would break if the code regressed to
returning raw e.code as the error field.

Ref: GAP-P3-33

